[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'A company from Singapore is giving away a frontier level AI model for free. Not a trial, not a stripped-down version, the full model with no usage cap, and they say it stays free indefinitely. So, let me walk you through what this thing'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is, because the road map here is honestly the most interesting part. The model is called Agnes. It comes from a company called Sapiens AI, and Sapiens is Singapore\'s own homegrown model lab. That part matters more than it sounds.'

[00:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'For the last few years, the whole AI race has basically been America versus China. Open AI, Anthropic, and Google on one side. DeepSeek, Qwen, GLM, and Kimmy on the other. Agnes is a third player'

[00:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'from a completely different place, and Singapore has been pretty open about wanting to build its own models instead of just renting everyone else\'s. Sapiens didn\'t build just one text model, either. Agnes is a full family.'

[00:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'There\'s a text model, an image model, and a video model, all under the same brand. The text model is Agnes 2.0 Flash. The image model is Agnes Image 2.0 and 2.1. And the video model is'

[01:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Agnes Video V2.0. On their site, they show the image model sitting in the top 10 on the artificial analysis image editing leaderboard with an Elo around 1178, right under GPT'

[01:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Image 2 and Nano Banana Pro. The video model is also top 10 on the image to video board. And the text model ranks number nine on a benchmark called Claw'

[01:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Eval with a pass score of 60.9% ahead of models like GPT 5.4 and DeepSeek V4 Pro on that board. So, these are not throwaway models. They benchmark'

[01:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'next to the big names, and all three of them are free. That\'s the core pitch. No waitlist, no subscription, no hidden meter that cuts you off after a few messages. The company says they built'

[01:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this for developers who got priced out, whether that\'s token costs, API limits, or just living in the wrong country. The previous generation already had over 585,000'

[02:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'developers using it through the API, so this isn\'t an empty launch either. There\'s a real crowd building on it. Also, Sapiens announced Agnes 2.5 Flash, the next generation of the text model.'

[02:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'It\'s not released yet. It\'s coming soon with a phased rollout and API access planned to follow. It\'s built for coding and agentic work, meaning you give it a goal and it plans the steps, edits'

[02:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'files, runs commands, and checks its own output instead of waiting for you between every message. And it\'s going to stay free, same as the current model. That\'s the part I keep coming back to.'

