VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'aimed at long-running agent tasks, large code bases, and heavy engineering work, and they\'re openly positioning it against Claude Opus 4.8 and GLM 5.2. Pro will be the premium paid tier when it'

[03:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'lands. So, the lineup is simple. 2.0 Flash is free and live today. 2.5 Flash is the free upgrade coming soon, and 2.5 Pro is the paid heavyweight after that.'

[03:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'There\'s also a desktop app called Agnes Code. It\'s kind of like Claude Code, but with a GUI instead of a terminal. You point it at a project folder, type what you want in plain English, and it'

[03:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'works directly inside your real files. It reads the project structure, edits across multiple files, runs commands, and saves everything to the project instead of dumping code into a chat window you have to copy from.'

[03:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'There\'s a smart mode toggle, a model picker, and support for skills, so you can invoke custom instructions with a dollar sign, reference files with the at symbol, and run commands with a slash. The new 2.5 flash model is set to go'

