AUDIO: 'The chart rendered, the numbers updated when I edited the data, and the whole thing took a few minutes. First draft quality, sure, but a usable first draft from one prompt at zero cost is the'

[05:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'point. Then, I pushed it harder. I asked for a small browser game, a brick breaker clone with a score counter, three levels, and increasing ball speed. Games are a good stress test because'

[05:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'they have state, collision logic, timing, and rendering all tangled together. If a model can hold all of that together from a single description, everyday web work becomes trivial for it. The model got the game running on'

[05:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the first pass. The paddle controls felt slightly off, so I said the paddle feels slow, make it snappier, and it went back into the code and fixed just that part without breaking anything else. That'

[05:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'back-and-forth loop is where these tools either earn your trust or lose it, and this one held up. And remember, this is the old model. The 2.5 version is supposed to beat it on every test they'

[06:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'ran. Sapien shared a chart comparing Agnes 2.5 Pro, 2.5 Flash, and the current 2.0 Flash against Claude Opus 4.8, GLM 5.2, DeepSeek v1.4 Pro, and Qwen 3.5. On SWE-Bench Verified, which'

[06:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
